From: stupidmonk37 <198526109+stupidmonk37@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpsd: pass each configured device as its own argument

The gpsd init script quotes "$device", so a uci value naming two sources
("/dev/pps0 /dev/ttymxc0") reaches gpsd as one path with a space in it and
gpsd opens neither. Venice boards deliver GNSS PPS on a CPU GPIO
(pps-gpio, /dev/pps0) rather than on the GNSS UART's DCD line, so gpsd only
sees the PPS when /dev/pps0 is listed as a separate source.

---
diff --git a/feeds/packages/utils/gpsd/files/gpsd.init b/feeds/packages/utils/gpsd/files/gpsd.init
--- a/feeds/packages/utils/gpsd/files/gpsd.init
+++ b/feeds/packages/utils/gpsd/files/gpsd.init
@@ -29,7 +29,11 @@
 
 	[ "$listen_globally" -ne 0 ] && procd_append_param command -G
 	procd_append_param command -S "$port"
-	procd_append_param command "$device"
+	# "device" may name several sources, e.g. "/dev/pps0 /dev/ttymxc0" on a
+	# board whose PPS arrives on a GPIO rather than the tty's DCD line; gpsd
+	# needs each as its own argument.
+	# shellcheck disable=SC2086
+	procd_append_param command $device
 	procd_set_param respawn
 
 	procd_close_instance
